  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves analyzing restaurant ratings data to gain insights into the performance of various dining establishments. The focus is on using SQL to extract, transform, and analyze the dataset, identifying factors that impact a restaurant's rating. The dataset includes information about consumers and restaurants, covering multiple variables such as location, cuisine, and price range.\n\n Objectives\n\n1. Extract and analyze data to understand factors influencing restaurant ratings.\n2. Perform sentiment analysis to identify well-reviewed restaurants.\n3. Provide strategic recommendations for restaurants to enhance performance.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Restaurant Owners: Seek insights to improve their services and customer satisfaction.\n- Data Analysts: Perform the analysis and generate reports and recommendations.\n- Marketing Teams: Use insights to tailor promotional strategies based on customer preferences.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Extraction & Transformation: Utilize SQL to handle extraction and transformation of data from multiple tables.\n2. Rating Analysis: Analyze ratings based on factors such as location, cuisine, and price.\n3. Sentiment Analysis: Conduct sentiment analysis to determine customer satisfaction levels.\n4. Report Generation: Produce comprehensive reports detailing insights and recommendations.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Ensure the system efficiently processes large datasets to produce timely insights.\n- Scalability: Support the potential increase in data volume as more ratings and consumer information are added.\n- Data Security: Safeguard sensitive consumer and restaurant information, adhering to privacy standards.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0221\nCREATE TABLE `consumer` (\n  `consumer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`consumer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant` (\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `restaurant_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `cuisine` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price_range` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` decimal(3,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sentiment_score` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `rating` (\n  `rating_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `consumer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating_value` decimal(3,2) NOT NULL,\n  `review_text` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sentiment_label` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rating_id`),\n  KEY `rating_ibfk_1` (`consumer_id`),\n  KEY `rating_ibfk_2` (`restaurant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `rating_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`consumer_id`) REFERENCES `consumer` (`consumer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `rating_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`restaurant_id`) REFERENCES `restaurant` (`restaurant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
